arge colander and slowly pour the kettleful of boiling water over the leaves to wilt them. Leave to drain for a few moments, then share between 4 warm plates. Arrange the fish on top, and place a poached egg onto each portion.", "Sprinkle with black pepper and serve with the tomatoes and toast."], "lines": [{"raw": "4 haddock", "name": "haddock", "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "4 tomatoes, halved", "name": "tomatoes", "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "prep_note": "halved", "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "4 eggs", "name": "eggs", "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "4 slices whole wheat bread", "name": "whole wheat bread", "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "slices", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "4 teaspoons margarine", "name": "margarine", "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "teaspoon", "prep_note": "low fat", "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "300g spinach", "name": "spinach", "quantity": 300.0, "unit": "gram", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "1 pinch ground black pepper", "name": "black pepper", "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "pinch", "prep_note": "ground", "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}]}, {"slug": "panjabi-dhal", "title": "Panjabi dhal", "servings": 4, "prep_time_min": 5, "cook_time_min": 25, "notes": null, "nutrition": {"calories": 245.0, "protein_g": 15.0, "carbs_g": 28.4, "fat_g": 8.2, "sodium_mg": null, "fiber_g": null}, "source_name": "Better Health: Healthier Families recipes", "source_url": "https://www.nhs.uk/healthier-families/recipes/panjabi-dhal/", "source_license": "Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.", "steps": ["Put the washed mung dhal and red lentils in a large pot, add the water and put on the hob on a low heat. After a few minutes, add the salt and turmeric, stir and bring to the boil. Once boiling, turn the heat down again and leave to simmer, partially covered, for around 15 minutes.", "Meanwhile, heat the rapeseed oil in a shallow frying pan on medium heat. Add the cumin seeds and fry for 15 seconds, then add the onions and garlic. Once those are soft and beginning to brown (around 5 minutes), add the green chillies, mix well and cook for a further couple of minutes.", "Add the mixture from the frying pan to the simmering lentils, stir well and turn up to a medium heat. Once boiling, turn off the heat and remove the pot.", "Allow to cool for a few minutes, then top with chopped coriander."], "lines": [{"raw": "50g red lentils, washed and drained", "name": "red lentils", "quantity": 50.0, "unit": "gram", "prep_note": "washed and drained", "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "170g moong dal, washed and drained", "name": "moong dal", "quantity": 170.0, "unit": "gram", "prep_note": "washed and drained", "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "1.5 litres water", "name": "water", "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "liter", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "1 large onion, finely chopped", "name": "onion", "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "prep_note": "finely chopped", "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "4 garlic cloves, finely chopped", "name": "garlic", "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "cloves", "prep_note": "finely chopped", "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "4 chili peppers, finely chopped", "name": "chili peppers", "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "prep_note": "green, finely chopped", "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "30ml rapeseed oil", "name": "rapeseed oil", "quantity": 30.0, "unit": "milliliter", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "1 teaspoon salt (optional)", "name": "salt", "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "teaspoon", "prep_note": "optional", "is_optional": true, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "1.5 teaspoons turmeric", "name": "turmeric", "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "teaspoon", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "1 teaspoon cumin seeds", "name": "cumin seeds", "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "teaspoon", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "fresh cilantro, finely chopped (to serve)", "name": "fresh cilantro", "quantity": null, "unit": null, "prep_note": "finely chopped", "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}]}, {"slug": "panjabi-keema", "title": "Panjabi keema", "servings": 4, "prep_time_min": 15, "cook_time_min": 20, "notes": null, "nutrition": {"calories": 451.0, "protein_g": 53.0, "carbs_g": 9.2, "fat_g": 20.0, "sodium_mg": null, "fiber_g": null}, "source_name": "Better Health: Healthier Families recipes", "source_url": "https://www.nhs.uk/healthier-families/recipes/panjabi-keema/", "source_license": "Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.", "steps": ["Blend the chopped tomatoes, ginger and green chillies together, and set aside for later.", "Heat the oil in a non-stick pan on medium heat and cook the chopped onions for 5 minutes or so. Once softened and beginning to brown, add the chopped garlic and cook for a further 3 minutes.", "Add the blended tomato, ginger and chilli mix to the pan, along with the turmeric and frozen peas. Stir well and cook for a further 3 minutes.", "Add the turkey mince to the pan along with the remaining spices. Mix well and keep cooking on a medium heat until the meat has turned white. Cover the pan, turn the heat to low and cook for another 5 minutes.", "Remove the lid and carry on cooking for a few minutes to allow any excess water to evaporate. Once ready, top with chopped coriander."], "lines": [{"raw": "30ml rapeseed oil", "name": "rapeseed oil", "quantity": 30.0, "unit": "milliliter", "prep_note": null, "is_optional": false, "is_alt": false}, {"raw": "2 onions, finely chopped", "name": "onions", "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "prep_note": "finely chopped", "is_optional": false, "